#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134560 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67683e7d-bf4f-5fdf-8fe5-df996c30e836" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Vectors Is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bfe4101-1788-57a5-8ac1-2c57a2f6071f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460513} {:answer/id #uuid "6e71543c-7657-547f-a18c-7f2c9399f2e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e71543c-7657-547f-a18c-7f2c9399f2e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460514} :answer-field/id #uuid "df08f260-5444-5ae9-8d62-29e40a4e506b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be9b958-1cbc-5d5c-ab57-ff274247d9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460515} {:answer/id #uuid "9910ea02-2b27-5ca3-97ce-4b26453b65a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0be9b958-1cbc-5d5c-ab57-ff274247d9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460515} :answer-field/id #uuid "405cf54e-21d8-5914-a3f7-9997f14dd3b0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd98d551-abd5-51b0-9163-7cca51863f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460517} {:answer/id #uuid "6acd70ed-8270-5710-b977-1d407c3bc24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd98d551-abd5-51b0-9163-7cca51863f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460517} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ce29998-b7b3-5f9a-8e15-33f308175a0f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89d04c73-ac43-52ba-9b0d-f07e5d286354" :question/math-academy-id "q-98523" :question/problem "$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors shown above. Given that the inner product in the vector space ${R}^{3}$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{2}⟩ & =(6)(-1)+2(0)(1)+3(-2)(-1) \\\\  & =-6+0+6 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement II is false since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩ & =(6)(1)+2(0)(1)+3(-2)(0) \\\\  & =6+0+0 \\\\  & =6\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥̸{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${v}_{1}⊥̸{v}_{3},$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "382a6db7-2708-5711-885e-6f3f3037e8df" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Functions is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338f1d6d-db3e-5039-8b5f-aae22fabbd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460519} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0aa715-cd46-53c6-8496-e8659486cc4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "338f1d6d-db3e-5039-8b5f-aae22fabbd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460519} :answer-field/id #uuid "e072e774-4518-5103-b30b-43265d9155f3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461126} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63cc9190-0ae1-5996-a7f6-181e038cbfa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460521} {:answer/id #uuid "2fa45487-8b6f-5b57-a845-0357f250b036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63cc9190-0ae1-5996-a7f6-181e038cbfa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460521} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bad1972-2fc5-5c34-b0b0-ea00210ef3e4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "948e577a-3aef-54e4-b34e-06b35d762788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460523} {:answer/id #uuid "fef9594e-8ffa-5e45-92ae-7b0feb6eda72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "948e577a-3aef-54e4-b34e-06b35d762788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460523} :answer-field/id #uuid "42e7f608-b7d2-507d-802e-9a170099ff23" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461128}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a5307a8-8a58-5d9f-8aa3-c19ff22a65ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-98524" :question/problem "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,{f}_{3}(t)=t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[0,\\pi ]$ of continuous functions over $[0,\\pi ]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is called orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the identity $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{3}(t)⟩=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,t⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the integration by parts formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t){|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =0+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-2\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67683e7d-bf4f-5fdf-8fe5-df996c30e836" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Vectors Is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cd9f0e8-a24e-56ca-9b35-3d20cfaf108a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460531} {:answer/id #uuid "259c4552-e209-5c99-a5e6-bd6496de834a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "259c4552-e209-5c99-a5e6-bd6496de834a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460532} :answer-field/id #uuid "501bcedc-e9e7-5701-8822-63b288ec14e5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461132} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1177f64-3b06-57ce-8e76-cb501ace8944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460533} {:answer/id #uuid "19f13dcd-f1c9-5b3c-9af0-25c639ba91e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19f13dcd-f1c9-5b3c-9af0-25c639ba91e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460534} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1c8e995-7173-5c3d-abca-4ce5910c0c51" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dff2943b-54f6-5db5-b389-bb1522249521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460535} {:answer/id #uuid "04d21503-375a-5aba-bcd6-32a725fdf8a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04d21503-375a-5aba-bcd6-32a725fdf8a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460536} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ab9e1ce-f903-5879-9b70-776ebbe8c793" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f758f1fb-abdb-5749-9b81-10132d816072" :question/math-academy-id "q-99636" :question/problem "$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors shown above. Given that the inner product in the vector space ${R}^{3}$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+4{x}_{3}{y}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{2}⟩ & =(4)(-8)+(-2)(4)+4(2)(5) \\\\  & =-32-8+40 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩ & =(4)(1)+(-2)(2)+4(2)(0) \\\\  & =4-4+0 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, computing the inner product $⟨{v}_{2},{v}_{3}⟩$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{2},{v}_{3}⟩ & =(-8)(1)+(4)(2)+4(5)(0) \\\\  & =-8+8+0 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\nAs a result, the set $S$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147801 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147544 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "638e604b-5416-5d3c-a61f-5be645aa255b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "828f3b62-d6fc-55e1-890d-d6145d705ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459829} {:answer/id #uuid "539b6b66-f4ad-5922-9730-438128ba5b07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "539b6b66-f4ad-5922-9730-438128ba5b07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459830} :answer-field/id #uuid "69d15af5-fbb9-5372-a601-ae7f5758d4d2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263c2f5a-1877-5619-a24b-221f11d150a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459831} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1a5cd4-be57-5868-99a4-583204f33015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "263c2f5a-1877-5619-a24b-221f11d150a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459831} :answer-field/id #uuid "0678aeb4-97dd-5a0c-ba48-5da21cc51635" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84821ab6-88a8-5a73-bd50-ca06f607081f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459833} {:answer/id #uuid "3245b31d-675f-5700-81fc-86a8ab50e5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3245b31d-675f-5700-81fc-86a8ab50e5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459834} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad59991b-d7c3-5f26-ac4f-f72283e8c6f9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "436201f3-78ea-5cda-b175-c5331e2f77ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-348980" :question/problem "Lionel and David are youth soccer players. In the previous season, $12%$ of Lionel’s goals were scored from the penalty spot, while the decimal proportion of David’s goals scored from the penalty spot was $0.1.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Lionel's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\nII. More than half of David's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\nIII. Lionel had a greater percentage of goals scored from the penalty spot compared to David.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n12%<50%,\n$$\n\nless than half of Lionel's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.1<0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of David's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\n- Statement III is true. We can compare $12%$ and $0.1$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.1\\times 100=10%\n$$\n\nSince  $12%>10%,$ Lionel had a **greater** percentage of goals scored from the penalty spot compared to David.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147592 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7eacaa-2cf2-5cae-a40c-737c98124bcf" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Degree of a Homogeneous Polynomial Using the Fast Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0508b59a-38ac-5845-9d20-c09a88738f01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460113} {:answer/id #uuid "93f4fcf4-f6b9-5495-87c9-83f547210a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0508b59a-38ac-5845-9d20-c09a88738f01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460113} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0b3278-1ddc-5453-a650-b43b661debc0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ba2c592-f680-502a-ae79-73c72b9fbe14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460115} {:answer/id #uuid "d506ed5d-7d8e-56ee-983d-b4fc96ec8260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ba2c592-f680-502a-ae79-73c72b9fbe14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460115} :answer-field/id #uuid "d74975cf-f415-54ce-91b6-a557425643c1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f383072-ee80-5c48-a1fc-2afc627d9c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460117} {:answer/id #uuid "069fe36c-e578-53dd-8829-e41aa8493cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "069fe36c-e578-53dd-8829-e41aa8493cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460118} :answer-field/id #uuid "51936e04-8fc9-5dfb-965c-aade2b0b32fa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5a7e39d-2b55-5b19-ad1b-291a9a1c5223" :question/math-academy-id "q-64176" :question/problem "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n- **I.** $f(x)=2x+1$\n- **II.** $g(x,y)={x}^{3}+3xy$\n- **III.** $h(x,y)={x}^{5}-{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-{y}^{5}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $1.$ However, it also contains a constant term. Therefore not all of its terms are of degree $1.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $3.$ However, it also contains a term ($3xy$) that is of degree $2.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $3.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $5.$ It is a polynomial of degree $5,$ and all of its terms are of degree $5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "813ec1d4-93ec-5a9e-996f-b2e672714927" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae0d728a-3ed9-59c0-bc16-a6326b390184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460119} {:answer/id #uuid "67c5d6de-d4d8-5a7a-98df-4f104c50214b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67c5d6de-d4d8-5a7a-98df-4f104c50214b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460120} :answer-field/id #uuid "31b92d5a-7f08-5cf5-86e5-e515e214cad8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f30afbdc-9b43-515d-a4ed-7769dc321fc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460121} {:answer/id #uuid "649b9469-3d31-5c1b-b6d5-39234a5cbdd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f30afbdc-9b43-515d-a4ed-7769dc321fc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460121} :answer-field/id #uuid "14cddedc-34ee-53cc-91fa-a8961b32c778" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2156dc4f-97dc-50e7-b4f5-a8ef9b80ddcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460123} {:answer/id #uuid "f15b09dc-d6b7-5ab5-a6b3-532c4e6950b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f15b09dc-d6b7-5ab5-a6b3-532c4e6950b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460124} :answer-field/id #uuid "38145e09-ea30-542b-8037-479fb7ee2d35" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31bc7182-8785-59ea-9a66-360f3942567f" :question/math-academy-id "q-64554" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9y=10{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+{e}^{-t}$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)+{e}^{-2t}$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+{e}^{-t}$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The general solution to this equation is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$\nIt can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=9\\,⟹\\,\\omega =3.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha {e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =1.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)={e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+{e}^{-t}$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+{e}^{-t}$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+{e}^{-t}$\n\nOnly I and III match the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "813ec1d4-93ec-5a9e-996f-b2e672714927" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f3fb80e-bfa7-5017-a56d-069fd980c629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460221} {:answer/id #uuid "ccbb63c5-39b6-5a60-b691-07641148a928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccbb63c5-39b6-5a60-b691-07641148a928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460222} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8d99343-4b79-5f95-9d4b-e725afec1d20" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b7c0bf6-51dc-5572-a384-70e76b7378a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460223} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0fbdb1-55c8-5908-99aa-c9f1404ab684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b7c0bf6-51dc-5572-a384-70e76b7378a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460223} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f1c2b1a-f87f-5559-a10d-b8e0fa87b72d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460978} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23d55bea-a33e-52fd-80aa-c6b6b76ff7cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460225} {:answer/id #uuid "983462b8-1f79-5e9f-8972-909efa066fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "983462b8-1f79-5e9f-8972-909efa066fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460226} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca0fcf8a-28f2-50c1-8bf7-172d804d702a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9aa670fe-3757-54df-85dc-a7b3def25d33" :question/math-academy-id "q-79461" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion with damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+25y=17\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y={e}^{-3t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t)-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nII. $y=A{e}^{-3t}+B{e}^{4t}+17\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+17\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nIII. $y=R{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The general solution is the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution:\n\n$$\ny(t)={y}_{c}(t)+{y}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+25y=0.$ Writing down and solving the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm 4\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(t)$ can be expressed in any of the following forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c}(t) & ={e}^{-3t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t), \\\\ {y}_{c}(t) & =R{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ), \\\\ {y}_{c}(t) & =R{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{6}$ and $\\beta =\\frac{2}{3}.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={e}^{-3t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t)-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ y(t) & =R{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+ϕ)-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ y(t) & =R{e}^{-3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t+ϕ)-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnly I and III match the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147492 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e71c0c9-7dd1-5f09-a55c-96b5bed1ee9a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Differential Equation Corresponding to a Phase Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e6e4576-cb2c-5f40-a024-0b79d87ba611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460449} {:answer/id #uuid "26b14906-c7f3-5d7f-b0ad-99c28013e0d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26b14906-c7f3-5d7f-b0ad-99c28013e0d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460450} :answer-field/id #uuid "38c7ed42-808d-5461-8925-03413bd4c72d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461091} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ff26235-ad35-5b68-8248-700bc1d7a8cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460451} {:answer/id #uuid "707e809b-5526-5183-832e-8d66c5aae6cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ff26235-ad35-5b68-8248-700bc1d7a8cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460451} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c652fd-ac7d-5203-b330-84bd10a9ee1c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461092} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3964794a-ae53-591f-93de-d8ce066bcc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460453} {:answer/id #uuid "d18e5255-26c2-53ec-9ae8-fdfff869cd5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3964794a-ae53-591f-93de-d8ce066bcc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460453} :answer-field/id #uuid "34932bd5-c652-5539-b173-7a6c06a591cc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8c00e37-f5cb-5639-8ab6-118fe74f0e44" :question/math-academy-id "q-96513" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3a06bdc7a63a86651752ff70331010920d24728e7f4e4ad9f067eb860ebaf4b.png)\n\nConsider the phase line shown above. Which of the following differential equations could have this phase line?\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}-1$\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(y-1)^{2}(y+1)$\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(y-1)^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all three differential equations are of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThe phase line gives us the following information:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=-1$ and $y=1.$\n\n- $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (1,\\infty ).$\n\n- $f(y)$ is negative for $y\\in (-1,1).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's study each of the given equations.\n\n- We start by considering ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}-1.$\n\nFirst, we see that $f(y)={y}^{2}-1,$ so $f(y)=0$ if $y=-1,1.$ So, the equilibrium solutions correspond to those shown in the phase line.\n\nNow, we can construct a sign table for $f(y)$ as follows: \n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-1)$ | $(-1,1)$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y+1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $y-1$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is negative for  $y\\in (-1,1),$ and $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (1,\\infty ).$ This corresponds to the arrows shown on the phase line.\n\nTherefore, equation I has the given phase line.\n\n- Next, we consider ${y}^{′}=(y-1)^{2}(y+1).$\n\nFirst, $f(y)=(y-1)^{2}(y+1),$ so $f(y)=0$ if $y=-1,1.$ So, the equilibrium solutions correspond to those shown in the phase line.\n\nHowever, we note that $f(y)<0$ for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1).$ This does *not* correspond to the arrows shown on the phase line.\n\nTherefore, equation II does not have the given phase line.\n\n- Finally, we consider ${y}^{′}=(y-1)^{2}.$\n\nIn this case, $f(y)=(y-1)^{2},$ and the equilibrium solution is $y=1$ only.\n\nTherefore, equation III does not have the given phase line.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147494 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "680a42fd-9b70-5fb2-916c-d10b71b11d82" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using Phase Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cedae9a-23df-57ba-9498-e233fc5b8a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460455} {:answer/id #uuid "a406dea9-6965-5b43-884c-0305c92aa491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a406dea9-6965-5b43-884c-0305c92aa491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460456} :answer-field/id #uuid "c698e3e6-ea98-5e40-b1a0-a0ba53519e60" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f37bb2f-b0a0-57b5-8d3d-715827fbe072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460457} {:answer/id #uuid "e33355ed-5572-5a69-9c58-3d748b0ee078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e33355ed-5572-5a69-9c58-3d748b0ee078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460458} :answer-field/id #uuid "848f67b2-1e31-5208-8f82-12469bb85089" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461095} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef713b37-5123-5e25-811c-70cbeca41945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460459} {:answer/id #uuid "98f41a9a-d427-5df9-a10e-9c04d50e4ee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef713b37-5123-5e25-811c-70cbeca41945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460459} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d946468-9cf0-55a4-9642-a1a3ec3e9677" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4de3adcb-e14e-526f-9d74-b55f67fd1c9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96558" :question/problem "![](images/92/9230d847daa518edfaad43f6552a48c2b3cac9523a1e9ecad8624851080e00ea.png)\n\nA particular autonomous differential equation has the phase line shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=-1$ is a source\n- $y=2$ is a sink\n- $y=2$ is a node\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=-1$ points upward, and the arrow just below it points downward. In other words, both arrows point *away* from  $y=-1.$ This means that $y=-1$ is a source.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=2$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points upward. In other words, both arrows point *toward* the point $y=2.$This means that $y=2$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147495 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f13d25-8aaa-53fe-b649-79f759aca692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460461} {:answer/id #uuid "9b5118f7-bea8-56bb-9fa7-7066d9d15341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00f13d25-8aaa-53fe-b649-79f759aca692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460461} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ed60369-6527-596a-aa20-10745731f2e3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58384368-2e9c-513d-884f-c895ead26452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460463} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab5835d-dd16-5c59-b329-2d76fad3fea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ab5835d-dd16-5c59-b329-2d76fad3fea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460464} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c4a2a63-53b5-5ff5-adec-a8a211a46343" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e56d3d31-42e8-5b71-9337-634db804ceee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460465} {:answer/id #uuid "5632df88-4d15-5fcb-8683-ca20c35ee138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e56d3d31-42e8-5b71-9337-634db804ceee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460465} :answer-field/id #uuid "b652d627-c7ef-5e71-8927-79a18df27daa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68af5d21-8052-5193-93c5-650cda389ee6" :question/math-academy-id "q-96560" :question/problem "![](images/93/936d303dcc89c5c27e77fa3d7cfc8b63643284d9e203f176c9e0c5588c27e049.png)\n\nConsiderer the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=1$ is a node.\n- $y=-2$ is a sink.\n- $y=3$ is a source.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/69/69e895d4091075f6d50eb9e44dc027c342d1fe7ca0269224c9b6a019ab312c77.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=1$ is a source.\n\n- Statement II is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-2$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement III is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=3$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147495 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "176db625-da1a-53ac-949e-55f3f0f02815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460525} {:answer/id #uuid "9b36caa5-478b-579d-b994-8f98db209f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "176db625-da1a-53ac-949e-55f3f0f02815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460525} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b9900a-7f32-5b43-89de-641b61f163a2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4329aee6-282a-5a99-bc97-a39c4b48ee2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460527} {:answer/id #uuid "8194998a-61d5-536f-9d0d-9d85ecb0a5a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8194998a-61d5-536f-9d0d-9d85ecb0a5a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460528} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c794f5-4ce9-5e9f-b0ca-6e8adb83ce03" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79ffb909-adc7-5001-a73f-43c6abd9277d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460529} {:answer/id #uuid "bf898885-f33a-5c9f-ac14-44e8c5d7c54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf898885-f33a-5c9f-ac14-44e8c5d7c54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460530} :answer-field/id #uuid "c48f2b29-59ae-54f9-8722-c487a06f19d4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4bed661a-2056-50bf-bcd6-efc6ac7543e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-98753" :question/problem "![](images/97/97d1a6a7f167b29a12e2f586067f6d7fa3cb5afec0be0ae854512cfe5c968d42.png)\n\nConsider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=2$ is a node.\n- $y=2$ is a source.\n- $y=-4$ is a sink.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/7a/7ad82b4ff48bbf69efccf5a822c7013929224a1a6e6e63e1948ea9ea95dcc858.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=2$ is a source.\n\n- Statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-4$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0abad78-e492-5d09-a04d-bce54605c78c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37857c14-e9d8-5ff8-b371-453bdcccb1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459365} {:answer/id #uuid "39c98a6d-0b5b-56e4-a2d6-30cb920436ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37857c14-e9d8-5ff8-b371-453bdcccb1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459365} :answer-field/id #uuid "2880db24-3981-59f1-8156-a1eedd6e86dd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460549} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "114bd932-69e9-56f5-8f32-bd3d35462900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459367} {:answer/id #uuid "acc3af12-c7ea-5216-8ed6-4ca5dab78a07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acc3af12-c7ea-5216-8ed6-4ca5dab78a07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459368} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd568dc-05a5-58da-b3ec-6002251d7945" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47acaf3b-ff10-55be-bc1b-9101c802c80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459369} {:answer/id #uuid "c23b93b7-3a6c-58e0-b193-425d41fe60e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47acaf3b-ff10-55be-bc1b-9101c802c80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459369} :answer-field/id #uuid "d643dc1b-cb05-5416-ab2c-d769dada2c8d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86e7e59c-5f60-5647-9c15-90e1d3a1ac43" :question/math-academy-id "q-109113" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A$\n- **II.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A$\n- **III.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{2}$ of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ Recall that an *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$ \n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nFirst, we compute $A-3I:$\n\n$$\nA-3I=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-3I:$\n\n$$\n(A-3I)v=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-3I:$\n\n$$\n(A-3I)w=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-3I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "515bc565-71af-5221-9644-0aa83842a772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459371} {:answer/id #uuid "85ca1bc0-8767-5bbd-8c32-74c4ccecbceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "515bc565-71af-5221-9644-0aa83842a772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459371} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5bc38a4-b7d8-54fc-a15e-6051610958ae" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "add4fd71-0330-508c-967e-e91acae428b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459373} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6dc8f6-e3ff-57d2-80a2-3f7f19e8d919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "add4fd71-0330-508c-967e-e91acae428b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459373} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceea3f1e-528b-558b-9481-3e2b4047d516" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcd49110-f42e-5516-8b3e-d072308e4699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459375} {:answer/id #uuid "07449d7d-1c19-5c1b-918c-57445e2e3e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcd49110-f42e-5516-8b3e-d072308e4699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459375} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e971058-f913-5f6c-a9c3-556bd4e47f97" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7971d731-7317-51d2-bfe1-46fc4b23c3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-109117" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A$\n\nII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A$\n\nIII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A+3I:$\n\n$$\nA+3I=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A+3I:$\n\n$$\n(A+3I)v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A+3I:$\n\n$$\n(A+3I)w=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A+3I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0abad78-e492-5d09-a04d-bce54605c78c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbca469-a09a-5aae-9061-eaabaf47cb82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459383} {:answer/id #uuid "f24a4df8-1519-516f-987c-510381d92a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f24a4df8-1519-516f-987c-510381d92a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459384} :answer-field/id #uuid "54cfa585-bc9e-5739-a2b3-2cec274bc4a3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c36856-0511-53a2-b1e2-b7e4a2d0a856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459385} {:answer/id #uuid "d3640da3-5e4d-595a-bdba-1a90c3045d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3640da3-5e4d-595a-bdba-1a90c3045d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459386} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7056ce4-0dc2-5a6e-9a67-45ab92d795ee" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc576af0-e18c-56ef-afbf-731c68a1fc36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459387} {:answer/id #uuid "3a2ff2a7-9088-54bb-8657-c345c13ee7b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc576af0-e18c-56ef-afbf-731c68a1fc36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459387} :answer-field/id #uuid "8be9ee5d-49cc-51bd-876f-c730adca6226" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13d405ca-1969-5fbd-88a4-d12478e301e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-109500" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$\n- **II.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$\n- **III.** $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{2}$ of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ Recall that an *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$ \n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nFirst, we compute $A-2I:$\n\n$$\nA-2I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following map:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{\\,A-2I\\,\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, we see that $A-2I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $1$ step.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ (a.k.a. an eigenvector) corresponding to the eigenvalue  $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "590283a9-e891-5d0c-b51e-c560f3e54daa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459389} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f625c4-00e1-5289-b535-2b768c528b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6f625c4-00e1-5289-b535-2b768c528b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459390} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd0e91cb-f6f7-5c3e-bb8b-d1156e9e5bb0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba9c2356-d274-52ab-a056-4da50da53ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459391} {:answer/id #uuid "07882ba2-c232-540f-8fe0-c6653a895e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba9c2356-d274-52ab-a056-4da50da53ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459391} :answer-field/id #uuid "d425a32e-7f30-58d3-bb5c-b3c831df78c1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71977d8b-bf39-5b1d-8d7e-94b8041534c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459393} {:answer/id #uuid "1d00776f-5194-5977-b5af-d8769896ebd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71977d8b-bf39-5b1d-8d7e-94b8041534c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459393} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9dd487e-dc8d-5257-a09f-ba81a3aa1ca8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6f4f929d-c8e6-554e-bc37-364f30077a9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-109587" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A$\n\nII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A$\n\nIII. $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A+5I:$\n\n$$\nA+5I=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Again, since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $x$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A+5I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $3$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "575dccbf-d52e-5dd2-b80e-45c63714f303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459529} {:answer/id #uuid "418bea30-cd14-5069-90a1-572182d3998c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "418bea30-cd14-5069-90a1-572182d3998c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459530} :answer-field/id #uuid "f18459b3-fcb2-52b5-b3c8-03c91c6ac6e7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460631} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92a5b226-87e1-5bcc-9924-a64cb1a3cba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459531} {:answer/id #uuid "603b980e-c926-5a8a-bf43-ebed5422d4e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92a5b226-87e1-5bcc-9924-a64cb1a3cba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459531} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d2674a1-ade2-52de-8083-812d250b99dc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460632} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f536b65-945c-5069-ade1-ce17175a0b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459533} {:answer/id #uuid "97573cd7-4a82-50f5-b3ca-e92bff2279fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f536b65-945c-5069-ade1-ce17175a0b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459533} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbf7638-1805-5c9a-962c-88753c4aaa5e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1109475d-9e0b-5521-b99e-3e1bd3fbb649" :question/math-academy-id "q-133622" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e4b568fe2226154be401a2332c718f143954d98fdbd8a0c679fdb99fcdd47d14.png)\n\nSarah interviewed some parents, asking them how much time their children spend playing outdoors per day. The information she received is summarized in the scatter plot above. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There is only one child who spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n- There is only one child aged $6$ among those surveyed.\n- None of the children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $3.5,$ namely, $(5,3.5).$ This means that only one child spends $3.5$ hours playing outdoors.\n\n![](images/01/0103370189c7156f9677ca576e2480bc99314cd312702fca3ea3e50cb4f7287a.png)\n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $6,$ namely, $(6,2)$ and $(6,2.5).$ This means that there were two children of age $6$ among those surveyed.\n\n![](images/0a/0a8ca9628b48e643e1aa9e9f0216148881db237c2d29054b29f4377ad182503d.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, two children spend less than $2$ hours playing outdoors. Those children are represented by the two dots below the horizontal line.\n\n![](images/4d/4d9709c131045f2e440204f79ad3fd8ff22707312b0e99138da558393e8b7f6d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67c58a8f-8248-5a1e-bc1a-ca754ff1bf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459535} {:answer/id #uuid "a165f429-0191-5e83-9162-d845ecf57294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67c58a8f-8248-5a1e-bc1a-ca754ff1bf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459535} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ed19dd8-2331-58ee-8e63-5060c63df0a4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27072f06-b04e-5738-828a-97b69f152668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459537} {:answer/id #uuid "27d7d283-6013-5e3b-a892-3787a588a476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27d7d283-6013-5e3b-a892-3787a588a476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459538} :answer-field/id #uuid "79cb274f-9e25-59dc-936b-c4b047a0d929" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460635} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9232092-31bd-57de-b974-cc58445adee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459539} {:answer/id #uuid "041282ea-d595-54e1-9a5e-7b57ffe6c62c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9232092-31bd-57de-b974-cc58445adee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459539} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a0be3f-582c-5cfd-9a1e-7daefb5e53f6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35f73958-c27b-5887-a2cc-b747d3896473" :question/math-academy-id "q-134133" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b25aa3b36011df9f9a97ca55fce75b2bf53b6b35282d8d5896e348464d4bdd30.png)\n\nMr. Clark recorded the height and shoe size of the players on the basketball team he coaches. The information he collected is summarized in the scatter plot above. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one player has a shoe size of $9\\frac{1}{2}.$\n- Only one player is $195\\,\\text{cm}$ tall.\n- There are exactly two players taller than $185\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose vertical coordinate equals $9.5,$ namely, $(180,9.5)$ and $(195,9.5).$ This means that two players have a shoe size of  $9\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2058bf02025ff359b509db01022c5d2e956d67243094a33692b90d6f1c2eac8.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement II is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $195,$ namely, $(195,\\,9.5).$ This means that only one of the players has a height of $195\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\n![](images/b8/b8b4364dc5de11eed12840bc644b1392b36160adfdf739b96f282c2367d999fa.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement III is false. According to the scatter diagram, three players have a height greater than  $185\\,\\text{cm},$ represented by the three dots to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](images/aa/aaf6d496c56c3cdc5a47e1c09e7640d7a3caa05446a75b705c042a56c116cb98.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea0ec28-488a-5ed5-b23a-ee6a7c3b6152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459629} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee31146-f63c-561c-9fe7-0190988d5191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea0ec28-488a-5ed5-b23a-ee6a7c3b6152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459629} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a06e7ee-beff-537c-a848-af5ba595ae03" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460681} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e80f37a5-ace9-5a66-9242-1b1a70a7a1d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459631} {:answer/id #uuid "c718208c-45b4-518a-b74d-4db5340e01c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e80f37a5-ace9-5a66-9242-1b1a70a7a1d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459631} :answer-field/id #uuid "5329ad17-fa05-5f55-a20c-b80b5f880455" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "390547a5-6535-52a6-90d4-0ab8f3425b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459633} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e5daac-3bca-5c19-a1a9-7a49a6752cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4e5daac-3bca-5c19-a1a9-7a49a6752cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459634} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4747150-8f2b-5a96-b68d-c5bd579b15b1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3aa2864d-150b-53f6-8540-2485ff225138" :question/math-academy-id "q-172296" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $x=1$\n- **II.** $x<0$\n- **III.** $|x|<5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-3 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇏\\,(x=1)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-3,$ then ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0,$ but $x\\ne 1.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇏\\,(x<0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=1,$ then ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0,$ but $x≮0.$\n\n- Condition III is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇒\\,(|x|<5)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEach solution of ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0$ satisfies $|x|<5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152078 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7345a2-810f-5a35-aa01-092e40df06f3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91a67b3a-5073-54f5-83fb-1d4270c77ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459635} {:answer/id #uuid "00f1eb19-3a97-5e5e-bc4a-3d6f902f3b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00f1eb19-3a97-5e5e-bc4a-3d6f902f3b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459636} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed263a7-bdad-5fde-b2c1-a3b2c00e98d7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebd3a3c9-78a8-5b45-a7c2-e12e1f7c6ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459637} {:answer/id #uuid "e69723d1-75cb-53da-bce1-790336143d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebd3a3c9-78a8-5b45-a7c2-e12e1f7c6ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459637} :answer-field/id #uuid "dabd76d0-f9b1-5396-8d3e-7611c4cd25a2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "393de18f-a9ee-572b-bea2-0808a050367a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459639} {:answer/id #uuid "202bc9f8-4641-55e1-a52d-fb0650489269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "393de18f-a9ee-572b-bea2-0808a050367a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459639} :answer-field/id #uuid "43f5c05a-2aeb-5247-98c6-4a0b312f1cf7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1189e0d-f1d2-59f2-9035-c87ca64ef4f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-172313" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}+2n-3=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n- **I.** $n=1$\n- **II.** $n<0$\n- **III.** $|n|<5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2n-3 & =0 \\\\ (n+3)(n-1) & =0 \\\\ n & =-3,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=1)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=1,$ then ${n}^{2}+2n-3=0.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n<0)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2n-3 & =(-1)^{2}+2(-1)-3 \\\\  & =1-2-3 \\\\  & =-4 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|<5)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then $|n|<5,$ but ${n}^{2}+2n-3\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfdef795-e81e-55c2-9c40-b0592562b360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459717} {:answer/id #uuid "28adba75-3ba2-5de1-bdd5-d2a1d6361b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28adba75-3ba2-5de1-bdd5-d2a1d6361b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459718} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ce480b6-6617-54d9-ad65-d484f0eb7400" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b9fb294-83f5-513d-8c76-140d1249a9c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459719} {:answer/id #uuid "ca9f5620-0826-57cb-94c7-3bc826b5f4f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca9f5620-0826-57cb-94c7-3bc826b5f4f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459720} :answer-field/id #uuid "587c72ca-b75c-580c-9db4-bce4de9dedf5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460726} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2db4308-e16a-5148-81e9-6c4f6ba1ae2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459721} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6e62e4-faec-5caa-87b7-7466bb668966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba6e62e4-faec-5caa-87b7-7466bb668966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459722} :answer-field/id #uuid "85ef0dd2-5351-57a9-b874-e14ffede21c7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d29be98-2715-5cb8-9c47-f3d0747dc8c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459723} {:answer/id #uuid "73b59ac6-4ce5-594a-92f2-9189d2014d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73b59ac6-4ce5-594a-92f2-9189d2014d47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459724} :answer-field/id #uuid "5210d7f9-8d8a-5c74-b113-64a5686f2ca5" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2a24748-f2b1-5dae-9e25-ddb47fe6a36a" :question/math-academy-id "q-214134" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A$ containing all possible triangles in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≅y\n$$\n\nRecall that $x≅y$ means that $x$ and $y$ are congruent.\n\nWhich of the following are true?\n- **I.** $R$ is reflexive\n- **II.** $R$ is symmetric\n- **III.** $R$ is transitive\n- **IV.** $R$ is an equivalence relation\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $x\\in A,$ we have $x≅x.$ Every triangle is congruent with itself.\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x≅y,$ then $y≅x.$ To see why, note that if we can find a sequence of rigid motions in the plane that maps $x$ to $y$ (implying $x≅y),$ then we can always find a sequence of rigid motions that maps $y$ to $x.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x≅y,$ and $y≅z,$ then $x≅z.$ To see why, note that if we can find a sequence of rigid motions in the plane that maps $x$ to $y$ (implying $x≅y)$ and another sequence that maps $y$ to $z,$ then we can always find a sequence that maps $x$ to $z.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, III, and IV.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01457e13-545a-541f-acce-7e047fbcc408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459799} {:answer/id #uuid "87fffe77-2143-5ff9-a2da-d1695227d7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87fffe77-2143-5ff9-a2da-d1695227d7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459800} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5a869e-488e-5c2d-b679-699f90c7fb17" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c86362a-34b4-52d6-ad75-a83bcdd09134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459801} {:answer/id #uuid "f98b348b-31e2-5430-8135-c980ff086ccb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f98b348b-31e2-5430-8135-c980ff086ccb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459802} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd47a839-63c4-5a6d-b3f2-177b46628555" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d15df765-6a00-5bd1-8191-5dfbfb9a0320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459803} {:answer/id #uuid "41ca8881-af27-5681-851a-1d131d4cd84d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d15df765-6a00-5bd1-8191-5dfbfb9a0320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459803} :answer-field/id #uuid "2930a8aa-b164-5efa-ac05-ac74a56ddd9f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5244118-e12b-5ac2-ae1e-3e2ab9060947" :question/math-academy-id "q-333520" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n- **II.** ${y}_{2}(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n- **III.** The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, we find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement II is true. First, we find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement III is false. Both ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of the equation. To check if these functions are linearly independent, we compute the Wronskian:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the  Wronskian equals $0$ for all $x\\in R,$ the functions are not linearly independent. Hence, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ don't form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1e82711-ac51-5228-a804-1fa990c75224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459805} {:answer/id #uuid "863f65d1-6c09-5fc7-9229-f2192ef8b701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "863f65d1-6c09-5fc7-9229-f2192ef8b701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459806} :answer-field/id #uuid "782a33f2-c589-5a92-89c3-730260ecc10a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d25a391a-473d-59a2-a939-6f566cc09ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459807} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ed9d3b-064f-5134-a779-fd16eac2b208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d25a391a-473d-59a2-a939-6f566cc09ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459807} :answer-field/id #uuid "48062bbd-ee12-5738-a47f-04a9032c16f2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460770} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a6bdefd-4eb4-5101-b957-85e5319b7fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459809} {:answer/id #uuid "92b100bd-b5bc-5ebe-a3ef-e3746c7a2aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a6bdefd-4eb4-5101-b957-85e5319b7fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459809} :answer-field/id #uuid "f03c3346-2011-57c2-9e66-8f81c201e4aa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e7ec306-a94e-573b-92ac-0141248c8937" :question/math-academy-id "q-333522" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+6y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the equation.\n- **II.** ${y}_{2}(x)=1+{e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the equation.\n- **III.** The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{-x} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & ={e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}+7(-{e}^{-x})+6{e}^{-x} & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement II is false. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{-x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & ={e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}+7(-{e}^{-x})+6(1+{e}^{-x}) & =0 \\\\ 6 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is not a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${y}_{2}(x)$ is not a solution of the given differential equation, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ don't form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Initial Value Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e77d06e-75de-5efc-a31a-08ab5cd28827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460125} {:answer/id #uuid "d7273db4-f030-554b-9eb4-1f8ad7088e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7273db4-f030-554b-9eb4-1f8ad7088e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460126} :answer-field/id #uuid "7255451a-6f73-5904-b058-7ec744515ab6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1476747-7cd7-5321-b84b-6e1235b6e7e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460127} {:answer/id #uuid "f91c9644-913e-582a-adaf-b144e1e7ea1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1476747-7cd7-5321-b84b-6e1235b6e7e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460127} :answer-field/id #uuid "e14339dc-b2b5-545f-aa5f-519565543cd4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da02e26-cd27-5a84-95fc-65e7c16865c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460129} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f92fd3-cff0-5229-b161-7053c1989dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da02e26-cd27-5a84-95fc-65e7c16865c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460129} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf992f83-6c65-58e9-a6aa-5bc334f98c34" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c0602e3-c50d-5991-b1fc-f704c082ddef" :question/math-academy-id "q-65014" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n- **I.** $x{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y={x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1$\n- **II.** ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=10$\n- **III.** ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-4x{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$).\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bc95a3-4e0c-5487-8427-31cee0ecf80b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions of Linear ODEs Using the Sum Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75241296-7d49-5ca1-956a-c38b114182cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460131} {:answer/id #uuid "fd89f6a8-704b-542d-b4cf-4a6f6fe0111a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd89f6a8-704b-542d-b4cf-4a6f6fe0111a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460132} :answer-field/id #uuid "6099e4a8-ed0b-5342-8225-9b646ac9e526" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460932} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9816c67-e577-5ad4-b7f8-b456b0361276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460133} {:answer/id #uuid "27592d46-4cea-5d31-b285-b1e4f988dacd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9816c67-e577-5ad4-b7f8-b456b0361276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460133} :answer-field/id #uuid "54550bb8-14b1-57b6-b59e-e95e4bbdf6c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "894e7a98-0c2b-5873-8c77-7c3eb7d45b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460135} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7bffe3-1408-59e7-ba58-734114cb573e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "894e7a98-0c2b-5873-8c77-7c3eb7d45b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460135} :answer-field/id #uuid "44abc534-51c3-532d-b919-1296780151a3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03be4c64-335b-58c9-94d2-aea65ff76ae9" :question/math-academy-id "q-65077" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ are solutions to the equation ${y}^{″}-3{y}^{′}+2y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n- **I.** $y(x)={e}^{x}+{e}^{2x}$\n- **II.** $y(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{2x}$\n- **III.** $y(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, then $y(x)={y}_{1}(x)+{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)={e}^{x}+{e}^{2x}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.\n\n- The function $y(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{2x}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the products of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the quotients of the known solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dacfbca6-6135-5d51-a07e-627fce79dfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b8a3121-c55a-53c7-b85d-0d7cc04d7d29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460197} {:answer/id #uuid "00b6d4c4-56c3-5ee1-8ac1-829a4efc942a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00b6d4c4-56c3-5ee1-8ac1-829a4efc942a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460198} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb9bbb4-a63c-5a79-bf32-93b2e53d24ec" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eac28bb6-8d8b-59a9-b7e9-41f288d9ed10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460199} {:answer/id #uuid "3e351bb2-929c-546f-96f1-8200b0d06341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e351bb2-929c-546f-96f1-8200b0d06341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460200} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fe8ced8-6627-5358-839d-26c7a572c952" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460966} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec7797a-5231-5617-bda8-babbfffb3f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460201} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0b73dc-aba2-5005-a4d2-809c22405838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec7797a-5231-5617-bda8-babbfffb3f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460201} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8c3a302-4930-5c70-a406-af398dd21cf8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57bb64c1-83a8-5ad6-a9bc-3ab2aa9fabbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-76893" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $C,$ defined by $x∼y$ if ${x}^{4}={y}^{4}.$ Which of the following equivalence classes contain the element $i?$\n\nI. $[-1]$\n\nII. $[-i]$\n\nIII. $[2i]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We have $i\\in [x]$ if $i∼x.$ Using the definition of the given equivalence relation, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{4} & ={x}^{4} \\\\ 1 & ={x}^{4} \\\\ {x}^{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $i\\in [-1]$ because $(-1)^{4}=1\\,✓$\n\n- $i\\in [-i]$ because $(-i)^{4}=1\\,✓$\n\n- $i\\notin [2i]$ because $(2i)^{4}=16\\ne 1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e36ef6d-631b-52d5-8dcf-a3163bedefc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460209} {:answer/id #uuid "bd99744b-e643-5e94-8726-2bfacb366109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd99744b-e643-5e94-8726-2bfacb366109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460210} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b26e83-37cb-521c-b74d-33d58c0ea6f4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460971} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69a8cf14-62a1-52b7-8e43-d8191005ec7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460211} {:answer/id #uuid "20be12cc-42f7-55a8-bdf1-917eebf1a93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69a8cf14-62a1-52b7-8e43-d8191005ec7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460211} :answer-field/id #uuid "71fd13b3-1e85-56d2-837c-5fa3662e3c8d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afc96503-5873-5b58-841f-5c0a4fed324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460213} {:answer/id #uuid "1d61e050-7b0c-570a-8891-cdc5dab33f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d61e050-7b0c-570a-8891-cdc5dab33f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460214} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0cd9155-6655-58f5-95b3-349f13d7bad1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba3bb1ff-f2f2-5531-a68f-b27801ed7066" :question/math-academy-id "q-78598" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[6]_{9}?$\n\nI. $-12$\n\nII. $3$\n\nIII. $24$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[6]_{9}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $6$ modulo $9.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[6]_{9} & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡6\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=6+9k,\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{6+9k\\,|\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,\\,6-2\\cdot 9,\\,6-9,\\,6,\\,6+9,\\,6+2\\cdot 9,\\,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-12,-3,6,15,24,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-12$ and $24$ belong to $[6]_{9},$ while $3$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bc95a3-4e0c-5487-8427-31cee0ecf80b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions of Linear ODEs Using the Sum Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19ac0897-f919-5edf-bf78-26e13f92883d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460227} {:answer/id #uuid "5cac7a37-3782-5a73-b5ca-7a757aae2a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19ac0897-f919-5edf-bf78-26e13f92883d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460227} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f68fb17-bbf0-5de2-a733-f061bc57f907" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460980} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38299350-adac-58c2-b237-ae74f9e17918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460229} {:answer/id #uuid "d576b556-948d-5f01-85dd-7dbbbbb23e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38299350-adac-58c2-b237-ae74f9e17918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460229} :answer-field/id #uuid "f893192f-f2df-574d-b0f9-690d9e384ab5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460981} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88d4d6b6-5445-510e-9981-988d2a0d34df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460231} {:answer/id #uuid "70814542-0d28-542a-97d6-915bb53990c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70814542-0d28-542a-97d6-915bb53990c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460232} :answer-field/id #uuid "d26bf839-1097-5aab-ab35-a98e10712050" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46b25723-729d-510e-b94e-77440edfe286" :question/math-academy-id "q-79724" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear, second-order ODE, then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n- **I.** $y(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}$\n- **II.** $y(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- **III.** $y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, then $y(x)={y}_{1}(x)+{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a function and the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0829d4a-239a-5a8e-9c8e-3cdc76a993bc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions of Linear ODEs Using the Constant Multiple Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87ddde79-2216-55f9-a241-4e3672b694c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460233} {:answer/id #uuid "0b7a88de-d9d2-5ec0-a2fb-a186b71ec20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87ddde79-2216-55f9-a241-4e3672b694c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460233} :answer-field/id #uuid "e844d229-6b8b-51c9-b888-0ba89abf3b5b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460983} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eeab3a09-b1a6-5339-9628-ec71bce3f490" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460235} {:answer/id #uuid "c845b3e9-cf61-58a4-9310-d63f07f4f147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c845b3e9-cf61-58a4-9310-d63f07f4f147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460236} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f15e339-1689-5c7f-8cf5-50895397afc6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460984} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7904cf0f-78cb-5a70-8792-6d23e6d0e9de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460237} {:answer/id #uuid "d97c94c7-45b3-50e5-a408-e6bc7d86f4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7904cf0f-78cb-5a70-8792-6d23e6d0e9de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460237} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b85a7e-07f0-5732-a416-1ae1d52c3ca4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6e0c318-7db3-5a86-afe7-c1d5265937a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-79730" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is a solution to a homogeneous, linear, second-order ODE, then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n- **I.** $y(x)={sin}^{2}⁡(2x)$\n- **II.** $y(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$\n- **III.** $y(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the function ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, and $c$ is a constant, then $y(x)=c{y}_{1}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)={sin}^{2}⁡(2x)$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=-1.$\n\n- The function $y(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a non-constant function and a known solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f78d8474-b7db-5ba0-8689-12d453fbad7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460239} {:answer/id #uuid "d0bbc983-2258-5972-96b8-7f137a39e449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f78d8474-b7db-5ba0-8689-12d453fbad7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460239} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e76259e-cc28-59a9-ae04-a17677637170" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460986} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "412336dc-01af-52b8-82e5-1d35ce6a80fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460241} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa10937-de88-58d9-bb3c-1b823502fd3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "412336dc-01af-52b8-82e5-1d35ce6a80fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460241} :answer-field/id #uuid "49d1c497-51a6-5a06-b829-9044a6911447" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460987} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1224b958-4ce7-5572-b30e-6b81553dfae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460243} {:answer/id #uuid "0b37fb7a-7125-50a7-a5dd-3d0e07ca6d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1224b958-4ce7-5572-b30e-6b81553dfae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460243} :answer-field/id #uuid "67a5ad5d-8099-50e0-a241-4540894a930a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460988}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c274592-717b-5063-8a47-5f35487eca60" :question/math-academy-id "q-80091" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9df0c9dd8b76ac337b6110fc92019924ad2ee1c4cc0da8216c27709b641a8451.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\n- $f(-2)\\ne f(0)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is **one-to-one**\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the graph, we have $f(-2)=f(0)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Again, we have $f(-2)=f(0)$ but $-2\\ne 0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement II is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "624215ff-efdc-5b12-8d61-9d66371672d9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Valid Region to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cf6e101-1c00-5dcc-888f-de100272063d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460255} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0cdc02-828c-526f-9723-879cb6e53e5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf6e101-1c00-5dcc-888f-de100272063d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460255} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a16d756-eb72-5a8c-80ed-b4fa2d878c40" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a59cca7b-7a07-5681-bb35-879972b8cf4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460257} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb86fd3-31fb-5fde-a73e-a0990c2619c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eb86fd3-31fb-5fde-a73e-a0990c2619c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460258} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d34c30-34d3-5f7e-af12-639a809b093c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84b45c9e-0547-545b-aea3-c77384a3028f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460259} {:answer/id #uuid "2b279824-e156-5c5a-9bf6-7d6cdf3710e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b279824-e156-5c5a-9bf6-7d6cdf3710e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460260} :answer-field/id #uuid "896ab326-7a3b-5ff1-97b8-ad486bf6ecf1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e648a84-4fc0-5e89-9abf-3bfad9d2cf64" :question/math-academy-id "q-80266" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}xy, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nI. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,1]$\n\nII. $R=[-1,1]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nIII. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/73/736575dceb6969f8b45e4038f702ebc84347ab66a1a8e5ea5103840ddd61ba31.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}xy, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangle I does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangles II and III cover the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152200 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "100ab73e-3dad-5b15-9da2-d244c67bcc9b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b99d976a-f891-5006-b006-1f89b0aed82b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460261} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9e8db1-87d7-5816-a338-04d02f84dbe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9e8db1-87d7-5816-a338-04d02f84dbe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460262} :answer-field/id #uuid "8797be38-2755-5b03-9566-c909c3af6f17" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460997} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3bef40b-07d1-567e-a53c-086d7570c681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460263} {:answer/id #uuid "561e321f-7bb3-54a3-9484-d79887120eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3bef40b-07d1-567e-a53c-086d7570c681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460263} :answer-field/id #uuid "632f4f21-76a6-593f-87d5-e2ea2f58cd86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460998} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0bf614e-4003-5fba-acfe-eac707b4783b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460265} {:answer/id #uuid "537369b8-b99a-5260-b918-86b0e348c6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0bf614e-4003-5fba-acfe-eac707b4783b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460265} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5cb38e4-a3c2-56e0-91a3-3fb1f913c942" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f66ee2a6-cdd7-5b19-895e-1ea6e9717b7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80267" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}-6$ and $y=2-{x}^{2}.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-6,6]$\n- **II.** ${∬}_{R}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-6,6]$\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/76/760595b548b2327b9c7c44f336d2c0c2b6a69688c887587f162f8ff2ac5bb5ab.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ad76e6b-acef-5221-8852-71dc42625bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Correct Function Used to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e019259c-a480-51c7-adee-7e64d30db325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460275} {:answer/id #uuid "3c62bbae-8481-50c2-900d-f50750addcab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e019259c-a480-51c7-adee-7e64d30db325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460275} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed25a22e-c812-5c51-97bf-3f552b015487" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f843948-205f-56d3-9549-f072aa94f578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460277} {:answer/id #uuid "b8af677d-062c-5280-a8a3-61adf659040c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8af677d-062c-5280-a8a3-61adf659040c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460278} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f5cff7-ebff-5f64-bebb-f05d813e5cf0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd0c58ef-21d5-557b-b1f3-8d8357abcf16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460279} {:answer/id #uuid "31b0c3fa-e8ff-5c10-b771-f69f3886b0f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd0c58ef-21d5-557b-b1f3-8d8357abcf16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460279} :answer-field/id #uuid "43970d5a-70f7-5eaf-9c95-866b3155b96e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ca2c9d4-83c1-5596-b062-1537df902124" :question/math-academy-id "q-80425" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d09a23a1ae9f737c7f19ba83d6d20c3fbcea3c7deb71fa307264c90afabc6580.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/16/1620acdcfd3783df478322ebe5e81cb274d908db12d9c8bdc701fe21070b828f.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions I and III. Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(2,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function II equals $\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "624215ff-efdc-5b12-8d61-9d66371672d9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Valid Region to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "567abe3c-003e-5470-895b-6e4de6668d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460281} {:answer/id #uuid "42a6b8b5-f337-585c-81c8-58ef0adc78c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "567abe3c-003e-5470-895b-6e4de6668d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460281} :answer-field/id #uuid "539f1f0a-a5c7-5cf1-8dfe-991c5ed6a3c9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "229a4b0e-7cc8-578e-9c98-62c05f0575cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460283} {:answer/id #uuid "420109c7-1b02-5fdd-bd56-6921fde84d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "229a4b0e-7cc8-578e-9c98-62c05f0575cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460283} :answer-field/id #uuid "759a1a61-0534-5515-a7d7-778c990a26c4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a98d4383-44c4-517a-8eb0-cc5ae603ebcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460285} {:answer/id #uuid "0c907cc0-6af1-5efa-95fa-10890d40d058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c907cc0-6af1-5efa-95fa-10890d40d058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460286} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e48dc1a-6694-5774-95fd-e6de685299f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8098b383-f4a9-5d0e-9352-b359bad47678" :question/math-academy-id "q-80430" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d7db51d6af763e8853f815feb6e74b88d0ca9a19e79c42b3a42da4e8b088f93c.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x+y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x+y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles I and II do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle III covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152200 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "100ab73e-3dad-5b15-9da2-d244c67bcc9b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1afea180-a623-5a85-b2f7-e86ec0aa2f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460287} {:answer/id #uuid "37ec0378-1336-5e18-8d9e-83c6a502a0fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1afea180-a623-5a85-b2f7-e86ec0aa2f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460287} :answer-field/id #uuid "addbf166-da9f-5d67-867a-ae617fda5629" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbdc2167-31e2-5824-a7bc-793f6c423420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460289} {:answer/id #u