- ${∬}_{R}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-2,2]$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,4]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d4ea352-2a82-5ff5-8c08-b7f9a09929e6" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Disjunction Absorbs Conjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90bc18a9-9ac5-5d99-9097-173d1c4c292d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460299} {:answer/id #uuid "de222f35-2fc9-5ba3-b69c-c4f4c4523eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90bc18a9-9ac5-5d99-9097-173d1c4c292d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460299} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e3ed5f-1349-5ea1-b552-ce47ec76611a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46b4c104-0691-55d7-800f-a093d4f91f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460301} {:answer/id #uuid "697af936-ef79-56be-9a9c-0d3b49de07ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "697af936-ef79-56be-9a9c-0d3b49de07ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460302} :answer-field/id #uuid "f157cf86-106b-5088-94e3-cc16da581904" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b28cb575-a296-5861-8f95-bfec134ddf84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460303} {:answer/id #uuid "d299af8e-f498-57dd-9eeb-10c28d9498cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b28cb575-a296-5861-8f95-bfec134ddf84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460303} :answer-field/id #uuid "d26e9b13-0eca-59df-8e36-4ca0f21ed856" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2ca6bb7-dcf8-5600-9384-c5d2e8fe7476" :question/math-academy-id "q-81082" :question/problem "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $X?$\n- **I.** $X∨(X∨Y)$\n- **II.** $(Y∧X)∨X$\n- **III.** $Y∨(X∧Y)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nX∨(X∧Y)≡X.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $X.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $X.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Y∧X)∨X & ≡X∨(Y∧X) \\\\  & ≡X∨(X∧Y) \\\\  & ≡X.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∨(X∧Y) & ≡Y∨(Y∧X) \\\\  & ≡Y≢X.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157801 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4106fe70-b9df-5621-ba64-66703855aaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Law that Conjunction Absorbs Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f1424b5-5b66-5073-87d0-1aa859444eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460311} {:answer/id #uuid "6863ea72-aa28-52cb-af55-5a4103c49918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f1424b5-5b66-5073-87d0-1aa859444eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460311} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc4a67d5-90e7-55cb-b2e6-8c94e0730daa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461022} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d3bfc1-5db0-509f-8ac7-4f49a953c68b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460313} {:answer/id #uuid "7b1bcd18-9956-5f6f-8217-3f78