![](images/2a/2ae902b1cccc00b59401ecba306ef7f6f47e92f6439614c13c349283d9e763ff.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. On which interval is the extreme value theorem applicable to $f(x)?$\n\n- $[-1,2]$\n- $(1,3]$\n- $[-4,-1]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,2]$ is closed, but the function is not defined at $x=2.$ So, it can't be continuous at this point. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $(1,3]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-4,-1]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-4,-1].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6fd58e8-aaed-556d-888a-e6413102b169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460041} {:answer/id #uuid "81922915-68b9-5c54-8bee-784c6d39c2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6fd58e8-aaed-556d-888a-e6413102b169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460041} :answer-field/id #uuid "115e9b49-91a9-5c59-b043-b405028a08eb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "888077d5-4d82-5b5b-b8a4-3a038fc1dc89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460043} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2c41fb-497d-5e52-8591-3ab354912d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd2c41fb-497d-5e52-8591-3ab354912d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460044} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6e85c2-8629-572f-8e6a-e48e9eb0fb66" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3533d2b7-ddae-5ec8-a6cc-5bc6ad0e2a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460045} {:answer/id #uuid "68144902-7f34-51b9-8ac2-be7a5b881945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3533d2b7-ddae-5ec8-a6cc-5bc6ad0e2a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460045} :answer-field/id #uuid "f62c0f8c-c76e-5f5e-a218-b4bcdc54f373" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ee96606-8ba8-569e-8f90-21918ad24c63" :question/math-academy-id "q-47787" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y={log}_{2}⁡x?$ \n\nI. $(0,5]$\n\nII. $[1,5]$\n\nIII. $[0,5]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $(0,5]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[1,5]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[1,5].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,5]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on $[0,5]$ because this interval contains points where the function is not defined. In particular, it is not defined at $x=0.$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eede91c4-9099-55df-a803-f87895d9f51b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extreme Value Theorem to Piecewise Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80f70124-c2af-5ee2-b010-11aa7285d0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460047} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1a1354-5046-5b4b-9996-9e9aa5387d93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80f70124-c2af-5ee2-b010-11aa7285d0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460047} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e6caf9b-4980-529e-97b4-de8f4825f3e5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bfa2956-3ca2-54c2-95f5-1587e0995009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460049} {:answer/id #uuid "9c0dc7bf-2fa2-5fd5-bc3c-554429a21d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bfa2956-3ca2-54c2-95f5-1587e0995009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460049} :answer-field/id #uuid "08d86bc0-031b-56ef-9be7-e1e3067eb03e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460891} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf06108a-57f4-54ba-a053-e5138c94a590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460051} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f7b59e-3df8-5891-bd78-1c7831303d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf06108a-57f4-54ba-a053-e5138c94a590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460051} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e3ce31e-0b4e-56e4-9147-5055ff5d8219" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76bcbf01-0552-53da-87ac-24d7932ac118" :question/math-academy-id "q-47922" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,{x}^{2}+1, & x<1 \\\\ -x+2, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function?\n- **I.** $[0,2]$\n- **II.** $(1,2)$\n- **III.** $[-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nSo, let's check whether the function is continuous on each of the intervals.\n\n- Consider $[0,2].$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}({x}^{2}+1)=(1)^{2}+1=2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}(-x+2)=-1+2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the limits from the left and from the right of $x=1$ are not the same. Hence, $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous on the interval $[0,2],$ and the extreme value theorem is not applicable on this interval.\n\n- The interval $(1,2)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- Finally, consider $[-2,2].$ The only discontinuity of the function $f(x)$ is at $x=1,$ which is belongs to the interval $[-2,2].$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous on the interval $[-2,2],$ and the extreme value theorem is not applicable on this interval.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7f35540-d877-5eff-9e46-9439bd28ec69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460095} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4c483d-ffe3-5e86-98b6-c03e4155d047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f4c483d-ffe3-5e86-98b6-c03e4155d047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460096} :an