878" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=0$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$\n- **III.** The series diverges at $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{3}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{3}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-1,2).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-1,2).$\n\n![](images/03/03901ede0b4fadb59556c63aa4534b3a9e20c1e8188388e6256434ece03d9211.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $0\\in [-1,2),$ the series is convergent at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-\\frac{3}{2}\\notin [-1,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $2\\notin [-1,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165abac8-b78d-5d8b-9797-98764bec8a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459473} {:answer/id #uuid "9682a02a-0b80-592c-b204-2e00e64c9de0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "165abac8-b78d-5d8b-9797-98764bec8a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459473} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8082197-4ec5-5193-873e-90d47f00746b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e01fbca2-a092-5b1e-95d7-018e7d1f5edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459475} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8e7a9-c801-5eeb-bd2b-c483bdb34b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8e7a9-c801-5eeb-bd2b-c483bdb34b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459476} :answer-field/id #uuid "422cd737-9b8c-53f2-a0cd-c12e1ad7286c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbcc0ff-2235-56bb-aa08-904c6e3a229b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459477} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c4988b-246a-5c24-99ad-02a2f31d8f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c4988b-246a-5c24-99ad-02a2f31d8f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459478} :answer-field/id #uuid "07711a4e-3e3f-5c90-b74e-ec28eded9fbf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58d69dfd-31b1-5851-b7cd-9ea022ec672e" :question/math-academy-id "q-125380" :question/problem "![](images/14/145b9dcc1e52dec65d64245afa89fba77e0d0cda5a919b52009e2397f3f03e16.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/20/20121d30445c9e756f1c2c024713bc6cd6f0464cfcfc24df68bc30c766c4988e.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/0f/0ff98536c275458d68deabda91f56bf63e7c8f59f5ea79c68292332d8cd58d4f.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459479} {:answer/id #uuid "0f4b12aa-dfc8-5cf6-bb46-fa30cda83363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459479} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ebe448c-6d78-52eb-b87a-c0f6378a526d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3a5163-4335-5da1-a308-4afc6fa83343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459481} {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459482} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6785c8-4fa8-5419-98ef-b6ca891fd2fe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a7f457e-5e87-5921-9c97-354280faa2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459483} {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459484} :answer-field/id #uuid "5480c90b-6e84-5672-a102-83d8323aaae1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26c0cce0-6deb-59c6-a9c4-06e4698080d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-125381" :question/problem "![](images/50/501a3512fb4b8a1898c6dfb8816d587de4a0cd585991d9c92d2bb35d83a2853d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/4c/4c11b38f9e598e0cd8fc50715d2091e5bea48d188440ae8a99c84d66a6acb6b9.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/34/346007ae582fccdf4519a3d1cd50a467e19d5345238343a1311fd3348bbeb138.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a2d901-52dc-580c-b53b-e7be3980d2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459485} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd85d8b-be1b-575e-80ac-713251f2e060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07a2d901-52dc-580c-b53b-e7be3980d2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459485} :answer-field/id #uuid "68a91996-588b-523d-920f-19a0c8f2360d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460609} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "445c0216-e1b1-5dd3-8feb-cc822c3d9a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459487} {:answer/id #uuid "17e40de4-f646-5021-9351-81097f6cd6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17e40de4-f646-5021-9351-81097f6cd6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459488} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5092c7-0f51-5842-8bc5-c41ed85755e5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a377412f-eec0-5aeb-b5a0-47d4b28ce15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459489} {:answer/id #uuid "872e5857-37ec-5931-83c9-83ec8a9ea82a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a377412f-eec0-5aeb-b5a0-47d4b28ce15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459489} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe9a2195-fa09-5aad-adbc-06b68d958d2b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d320327-1d15-55df-b5dd-771fb0fd1831" :question/math-academy-id "q-125394" :question/problem "![](images/27/270e72ebedac3741e1b7086021b16dc0975ae9852d402673c8044a67f8f774fb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/db/dbb6dbdfabccf7a94c67781210238c647e6f3a2e428cb79c4debdbff5e124720.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/1c/1c5aa77b0a89e1fcb0782c9d969d3a81bbec47b004f07bd3a53ccd10e623ba6e.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8b6878-85b8-58eb-a242-cf54f14a0ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459491} {:answer/id #uuid "31fb75c7-a022-54df-a901-a9869c56eff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8b6878-85b8-58eb-a242-cf54f14a0ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459491} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e67b26d-312f-5124-b515-45ca803fdb86" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460612} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "310240c9-bca3-503f-87c1-b88b9a790c48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459493} {:answer/id #uuid "8acc9467-c049-5e2f-91a7-f70e0c1b40fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "310240c9-bca3-503f-87c1-b88b9a790c48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459493} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a84f387-e198-5acc-ae65-f1896114917e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9fa6a11-4b01-5ec8-98ee-ef928f01c5a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459495} {:answer/id #uuid "aefb95da-9bcd-543a-8c79-cce66b4132ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aefb95da-9bcd-543a-8c79-cce66b4132ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459496} :answer-field/id #uuid "c520ba73-5e23-574e-b441-acfbad776311" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "889fbef5-9dc3-5991-a476-ffe3c0711611" :question/math-academy-id "q-125395" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0ae64bf57444ac42ec5efed392471cbbac7b1e317bc1fb06b33bcd2038a2e3c1.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/bc/bc0121782b16d513d7d17d3741bd07ef1716e096bb2459fbda0cb841c7fd8b43.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves **clockwise** along $-C.$\n\n![](images/1a/1a6b109bc1da3aa7905b05f7f7902523b45fd51a65b97bec1328037bd6c0cfe7.png)\n\nSo, ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28492e5f-19b4-5757-9d39-0a839e1cd010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459497} {:answer/id #uuid "28528a48-293d-52d1-843c-d4